      "Before compiling your QR code, it is essential to understand that Google Maps supports several link formats, each serving distinct technical requirements. Choosing the right URL format ensures that your QR code opens reliably across all mobile devices and operating systems without broken redirects or security warnings.",
      "H3: 1. Standard Google Maps Share Link (maps.app.goo.gl)",
      "When you click the 'Share' button inside the Google Maps mobile app or desktop web interface, Google generates a shortened URL format (e.g., `https://maps.app.goo.gl/xyz123`). This format is convenient for quick sharing, automatically opens the mobile app on smartphones, and works seamlessly for standard storefronts and marked locations.",
      "H3: 2. Direct GPS Coordinates Link (Latitude & Longitude)",
      "For locations without a formal postal address—such as food truck parks, festival grounds, construction sites, outdoor wedding lawns, or park pavilions—using exact latitude and longitude coordinates is critical. The URL syntax for GPS coordinates is structured as: `https://www.google.com/maps?q=37.7749,-122.4194`. This guarantees that the smartphone camera routes the user to the precise geometric pin location on Earth.",
      "H3: 3. Business Place ID and CID URL Formats",
      "If you manage a verified Google Business Profile, using the exact Place ID or Customer Identification (CID) number ensures that scanning the QR code opens your official profile card—complete with customer reviews, photos, business hours, and phone numbers alongside the map location. You can format this URL as `https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:ChIJN1t_tDeuEmsRUsoyG83frY4` or use your Google review link directly.",
